  "bio": "State Representative John Lujan proudly serves House District 118 in the Texas House of Representatives, representing the hardworking families of South, East, and Northeast Bexar County. First elected in 2016 and re-elected in 2021, Representative Lujan brings decades of public service, business experience, and community leadership to the Texas Legislature. Chairman Lujan currently serves as Chair of the House International Relations Subcommittee and Vice Chair of the Appropriations Subcommittee for Articles VI, VII, and VIII. He is also a member of the House Committees on Appropriations; Trade, Workforce & Economic Development; Local & Consent Calendars; and the Subcommittee on Workforce. In previous sessions, he has served on the Committees on.",
